`maybeBind` and `maybeRebind`, and so [`ChangeImport`](https://github.com/openrewrite/rewrite/blob/main/rewrite-javascript/rewrite/src/javascript/recipes/change-import.ts), joined a member into any existing import of its module, whatever `with {…}` attributes that import carried and whether or not a `// @ts-ignore` sat above it. Moving `buildTime` out of `import {buildTime} from "./legacy.ts" with {type: "macro"}` gave `import {buildTime, gitHash} from "./build.ts"`, which drops the macro; a member now joins only a statement with the same attributes and no `// @ts-ignore` or `// @ts-expect-error` above it, and keeps or gets a statement of its own otherwise.

- Fixes #9789
- Fixes #9791

<details><summary>Import attributes: a moved member loses them (#9789)</summary>

`ChangeImport` moving `buildTime` from `./macros/legacy.ts` to `./macros/build.ts`

Before

```ts
import {buildTime} from "./macros/legacy.ts" with {type: "macro"};
import {gitHash} from "./macros/build.ts";

export const banner = `${buildTime()} ${gitHash()}`;
```

After (broken)

```ts
import {buildTime, gitHash} from "./macros/build.ts"; // ❌ buildTime is no longer a macro

export const banner = `${buildTime()} ${gitHash()}`;
```

After (fixed)

```ts
import {buildTime} from "./macros/build.ts" with {type: "macro"};
import {gitHash} from "./macros/build.ts";

export const banner = `${buildTime()} ${gitHash()}`;
```

</details>

<details><summary><code>// @ts-ignore</code> above the target's import (#9791)</summary>

`ChangeImport` moving `a` from `./old.ts` to `./m.ts`

Before

```ts
import {a} from "./old.ts";
// @ts-ignore
import {b} from "./m.ts";

a(b);
```

After (broken)

```ts
// @ts-ignore
import {a, b} from "./m.ts"; // ❌ also hides a's errors, such as ./m.ts not exporting it

a(b);
```

After (fixed)

```ts
import {a} from "./m.ts";
// @ts-ignore
import {b} from "./m.ts";

a(b);
```

</details>

<details><summary><code>// @ts-ignore</code> above the import that moves</summary>

Same move. Not in the issue, but the same join from the other side: the comment ended up covering `b`.

Before

```ts
// @ts-ignore
import {a} from "./old.ts";
import {b} from "./m.ts";

a(b);
```

After (broken)

```ts
// @ts-ignore
import {a, b} from "./m.ts"; // ❌ now hides b's errors too

a(b);
```

After (fixed)

```ts
// @ts-ignore
import {a} from "./m.ts";
import {b} from "./m.ts";

a(b);
```

</details>

Both rules also hold where the same join happened on the other lanes: a `require` under `// @ts-ignore` takes no member in, and a moved `export {…} from` joins a re-export of the target only with the same attributes and no such comment above it.

A comment counts as TypeScript reads a directive: `// @ts-ignore`, `// @ts-expect-error: why`, or one on the last line of a block comment. The comments above a file's first statement are read from the file's prefix, where the parser keeps them.

Adds unit tests for `lib/Service/Import/*.php`. Tests only; no production code changed.

## Classes
- **`ImportPosting`**: a new `ImportPostingTest` (8 tests). Until now this class was only exercised through the pipeline tests. It now has tests of its own for:
  - an unmapped account, which refuses the post before anything is written;
  - an empty opening balance, which gives a warning, not a refusal;
  - a customer without an email, which is left out with a warning, and suppliers, which are counted out;
  - an existing customer found by email, which is linked rather than written again;
  - a post refused by the engine, which removes the journal and customers it wrote;
  - a removal that fails, which is logged while the refusal still stands;
  - a refused reversal, which removes its reversing entry;
  - a reversal whose opening entry is gone, which names the missing entry.
- **`ImportPipelineService`**: a new `ImportPipelineEdgesTest` (3 tests). It covers:
  - the dry run's duplicate-relation warnings (kvk, then email, then name) and contacts without a key;
  - an unbalanced opening balance refused at post even though the dry run still matches;
  - an unreadable due date leaving an open item `issued`.

## Numbers
- 11 tests added.
- Statement coverage of `lib/Service/Import/*.php` (pcov): 819/898 (91.2%), measured on the whole suite → 864/898 (96.2%), measured on `tests/Unit/Service/Import` alone. `ImportPosting` goes from 101/124 to 123/124, and `ImportPipelineService` from 384/417 to 407/417.
- PHP unit suite (`phpunit-unit.xml`): 10087 tests / 1 failure → 10098 tests / 1 failure. The one failure was already failing before this PR.

